1
00:00:04,158 --> 00:02:04,258
Please contact turkision@gmail.com
for any inquiries

2
00:02:04,258 --> 00:02:08,548
NO LIVING CREATURE WAS HARMED
DURING THE FILMING OF THIS SHOW.

3
00:02:43,765 --> 00:02:44,985
Faster!

4
00:02:57,089 --> 00:02:58,049
Boran!

5
00:02:58,049 --> 00:02:59,942
We can’t reveal Kongar’s plan.

6
00:02:59,942 --> 00:03:01,452
You should leave.

7
00:03:01,769 --> 00:03:03,819
As you command, my Bey.

8
00:03:15,946 --> 00:03:17,776
Selamun aleykum, my Son.

9
00:03:17,955 --> 00:03:19,795
Aleykum selam, Bamsı Bey.

10
00:03:21,527 --> 00:03:24,327
My Bey, I couldn’t come to your wedding
because of my duty.

11
00:03:24,327 --> 00:03:26,587
May Allah make you happy and fortunate.

12
00:03:26,815 --> 00:03:29,065
I hope you live long
and have many children.

13
00:03:29,065 --> 00:03:32,155
Thank you, my brother.

14
00:03:33,145 --> 00:03:35,785
One’s legacy continues
to live with his kin.

15
00:03:35,785 --> 00:03:38,775
There'll be more than a wedding.

16
00:03:38,952 --> 00:03:43,312
The brave hearts want
to raise swords and shield.

17
00:03:44,468 --> 00:03:49,648
We are talking about a bloody clash here
but you're talking about shields and kin…

18
00:03:50,028 --> 00:03:51,358
My Gündüz...

19
00:03:51,358 --> 00:03:54,368
Kin or war...
Aren’t they both like marriage?

20
00:03:55,389 --> 00:03:56,599
So be it.

21
00:03:57,412 --> 00:04:00,192
Perhaps when we drive
all the troubles away…

22
00:04:00,952 --> 00:04:03,842
… we can talk about marriage in peace.

23
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:09,860
What about Böke?

24
00:04:10,134 --> 00:04:12,524
He did his part very well my Bey.

25
00:04:12,524 --> 00:04:13,714
What did he say?

26
00:04:13,714 --> 00:04:16,504
Alişar is going to fall into
our trap as we want, my Bey.

27
00:04:20,684 --> 00:04:24,404
So it seems Dündar Bey and
Bahadır will be escorting them.

28
00:04:25,583 --> 00:04:28,573
Nevertheless, he is worried
about their numbers, my Bey.

29
00:04:29,224 --> 00:04:33,454
He who fights for the cause does
not care about numbers.

30
00:04:34,248 --> 00:04:36,948
One day, we will attack with
stones on our mouths...

31
00:04:36,948 --> 00:04:39,478
... like Ababil birds once fought
against mammoths.

32
00:04:39,478 --> 00:04:43,398
Another day, we will become David
and kill off the Goliaths.

33
00:04:58,099 --> 00:04:59,249
Halt!

34
00:05:21,169 --> 00:05:24,609
Today, soil will be fed with blood…

35
00:05:24,609 --> 00:05:28,919
... and Erlik Khan with
death spirits, Osman Bey.

36
00:05:31,884 --> 00:05:38,454
So Balgay, tell me, how much
do you trust Böke?

37
00:05:40,293 --> 00:05:46,533
He is as loyal to me as a mangy
dog is loyal to his owner, Osman Bey.

38
00:05:51,281 --> 00:05:53,031
Then we shall begin.

39
00:05:58,446 --> 00:06:00,206
Listen to me carefully.

40
00:06:10,791 --> 00:06:14,151
Preparations are
almost complete, Dündar Bey.

41
00:06:14,429 --> 00:06:18,839
And my Bahadır is coming with
good news, hopefully.

42
00:06:37,251 --> 00:06:38,951
I lost track of Konur.

43
00:06:41,623 --> 00:06:43,603
As if the ground swallowed him.

44
00:06:47,977 --> 00:06:52,627
Then, we'll play with Osman's rules.

45
00:06:52,860 --> 00:06:58,580
We'll act as we fell into the trap Osman
is trying to lure us into with Balgay.

46
00:06:59,536 --> 00:07:03,536
But, they'll be the ones
who'll fall into the trap.

47
00:07:06,819 --> 00:07:07,939
How?

48
00:07:08,377 --> 00:07:12,077
Osman told Böke that he'll
ambush me in my encampment.

49
00:07:12,276 --> 00:07:16,276
Balgay and his Nöker's
will ambush my soldiers.

50
00:07:16,895 --> 00:07:21,425
They'll do it
just behind this hill.

51
00:07:22,274 --> 00:07:25,094
I'll wait for Osman here.

52
00:07:26,595 --> 00:07:29,555
Balgay won't even guess
that I'll betray him.

53
00:07:29,844 --> 00:07:31,824
They'll fall into their own traps.

54
00:07:32,274 --> 00:07:37,544
Böke will earn Geyhatu's trust back.

55
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:47,600
Its time to get rid of
the malice called Osman.

56
00:07:48,098 --> 00:07:53,298
He thinks we're the prey...
But we'll hunt him instead.

57
00:07:54,210 --> 00:07:57,800
I shall not be called Alişar if
I don't remove Osman's heart...

58
00:07:57,800 --> 00:08:01,100
... with the dagger
he took Batur's life with...

59
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:03,670
... and hang his hand in
the middle of Kayı Tent.

60
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:10,520
The Bannerlords use their
encampment as support units.

61
00:08:11,281 --> 00:08:16,261
Coward Alişar will stay in his
encampment until he figures things out.

62
00:08:16,559 --> 00:08:20,779
In the end, he'll attack
and try to kill us.

63
00:08:21,732 --> 00:08:24,292
We'll set up an ambush here.

64
00:08:25,725 --> 00:08:29,905
While Balgay is dealing with them,
I'll start moving.

65
00:08:30,628 --> 00:08:34,338
I'll ambush Alişar in his
encampment before he moves.

66
00:08:38,152 --> 00:08:43,062
Alişar will set his encampment up
as near the ambush location as possible.

67
00:08:43,865 --> 00:08:46,165
This is the place which
overlooks everywhere.

68
00:08:47,592 --> 00:08:50,722
We'll fight on three fronts.

69
00:08:56,235 --> 00:08:58,565
Where is the third front, Osman Bey?

70
00:08:59,639 --> 00:09:05,479
With Bamsı Bey,
we'll attack Alişar's mansion.

71
00:09:05,592 --> 00:09:07,402
We'll kill his men.

72
00:09:09,210 --> 00:09:13,210
Who are you calling 'us', Gündüz Bey?

73
00:09:16,114 --> 00:09:18,034
Sheikh Edebali's dervishes.

74
00:09:18,542 --> 00:09:22,032
They're all great warriors.

75
00:09:25,004 --> 00:09:30,604
Obvious that you you won't
let that dog breathe.

76
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:36,060
It's illicit to let a
poison-breathing dog...

77
00:09:37,270 --> 00:09:39,050
... live, Balgay.

78
00:09:43,983 --> 00:09:48,233
About the mansion...
The mansion is everything for Alişar.

79
00:09:48,375 --> 00:09:51,915
His reputation, honour...
And hareem.

80
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:58,280
The soldiers will do everything in
the city to protect the mansion.

81
00:09:59,356 --> 00:10:01,216
There will be a lot of blood.

82
00:10:02,325 --> 00:10:04,475
There will be a lot of blood.

83
00:10:09,530 --> 00:10:11,730
The trees of liberty are
watered with blood.

84
00:10:12,761 --> 00:10:17,881
If they stay back and ask for mercy,
then our anger will also stay back.

85
00:10:18,911 --> 00:10:25,741
But it's our duty to cut the blades
they're trying to cut us with.

86
00:10:26,293 --> 00:10:32,173
Its time to feed our weapons with blood.

87
00:10:36,667 --> 00:10:40,017
You know where to find me
once we're done, Osman Bey.

88
00:11:25,950 --> 00:11:27,670
The child's birth...

89
00:11:28,145 --> 00:11:30,025
... we've been dreaming of...

90
00:11:30,644 --> 00:11:32,834
... and suffering from...

91
00:11:33,845 --> 00:11:35,315
... is today.

92
00:11:37,696 --> 00:11:41,306
We take our fame
from our ancestors...

93
00:11:41,918 --> 00:11:46,508
... and today, we'll pass it
to our grandchildren!

94
00:11:51,645 --> 00:11:55,645
Since we came here for holy war...

95
00:11:56,081 --> 00:12:03,041
... then we'll form a unit whose only
desire will be holy war, shaded...

96
00:12:03,041 --> 00:12:05,071
... and justice.

97
00:12:06,124 --> 00:12:08,094
We'll establish a Beylic.

98
00:12:08,377 --> 00:12:10,177
We'll establish...

99
00:12:10,419 --> 00:12:12,199
... a state.

100
00:12:16,166 --> 00:12:22,566
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

101
00:12:23,218 --> 00:12:29,978
Dündar Bey. You will go to the place where
Osman will set up an ambush with Bahadır.

102
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:35,390
As the Bey, my soldiers will be
under your command.

103
00:12:35,755 --> 00:12:43,015
With Böke, I'll hunt Osman who swore
to attack me in my encampment.

104
00:12:43,501 --> 00:12:48,591
Water follows water,
blood follows blood, Alişar Bey.

105
00:12:48,861 --> 00:12:54,591
Osman is mine. He still has
my son Batur's blood on his hands.

106
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:03,670
Dündar Bey...
I too, want to take Osman's life.

107
00:13:04,041 --> 00:13:09,901
But we need to hold him before Geyhatu
when he comes here.

108
00:13:10,090 --> 00:13:15,390
We can't get our point across
if Geyhatu doesn't hear for himself.

109
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:19,414
What if Geyhatu doesn't
give him back to us?

110
00:13:19,414 --> 00:13:25,544
What if he kills Osman himself? Then
what'll happen to my revenge, Alişar Bey?

111
00:13:25,544 --> 00:13:30,254
I'm after the hyena,
you're after the leather.

112
00:13:31,016 --> 00:13:36,576
It'll be as I say.
But if you don't care about what I say...

113
00:13:38,146 --> 00:13:40,856
... go back to where you came from.

114
00:13:41,562 --> 00:13:43,842
Father!
Alişar Bey!

115
00:13:44,862 --> 00:13:46,631
It's not the time to fight!

116
00:13:52,490 --> 00:13:55,780
I understand your pain, Dündar Bey.
But...

117
00:13:56,478 --> 00:14:04,928
This dagger will enforce its rule.
Doesn't matter if Osman is dead or Alive.

118
00:14:06,121 --> 00:14:08,071
Keep a stiff upper lip.

119
00:14:15,222 --> 00:14:20,542
You're right, Alişar Bey.
We need his dead body.

120
00:14:21,679 --> 00:14:28,569
It's enough if I see vultures
eating Osman's corpse.

121
00:14:50,822 --> 00:14:52,872
- Gonca!
- Bala!

122
00:14:53,376 --> 00:14:55,246
Welcome, my daughter.

123
00:14:55,856 --> 00:14:57,876
Thank you, Selcan Hatun.

124
00:15:01,710 --> 00:15:03,040
My Bala!

125
00:15:04,188 --> 00:15:06,768
Gathering supplies for
the lodge took long.

126
00:15:08,416 --> 00:15:12,646
I couldn't make it to your wedding.
But we'll be together in the feast.

127
00:15:12,646 --> 00:15:16,476
- Hopefully, my Gonca. Welcome.
- Thank you, Bala.

128
00:15:17,012 --> 00:15:18,672
Come on!

129
00:15:37,784 --> 00:15:39,134
My Sheikh!

130
00:15:41,762 --> 00:15:43,852
We've prepared the dowry, my Sheikh.

131
00:15:44,292 --> 00:15:46,292
We'll go to the Tent if you allow us.

132
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:49,620
These dowries are temporary, Selcan Hatun.

133
00:15:50,078 --> 00:15:51,918
We'll send it with someone.

134
00:15:52,794 --> 00:15:57,664
The real dowries of those who have...

135
00:15:58,144 --> 00:16:00,864
... strong faith, are shaded.

136
00:16:01,883 --> 00:16:05,883
This is the day of Ahiyans, Bacıyans.

137
00:16:06,333 --> 00:16:08,333
The duty waits for you.

138
00:16:10,576 --> 00:16:13,046
Give us your orders, my Sheikh.

139
00:16:13,749 --> 00:16:17,749
Osman Bey is on the road for a holy war.

140
00:16:18,504 --> 00:16:21,434
He's after liberty and justice.

141
00:16:22,131 --> 00:16:26,821
Supporting him in his cause is
the reason of life for us.

142
00:16:27,667 --> 00:16:29,767
What's our duty, my Sheikh?

143
00:16:29,767 --> 00:16:32,877
You'll join the attack
to Alişar's mansion.

144
00:16:33,687 --> 00:16:39,597
You'll destroy that origin of unrest.

145
00:16:40,391 --> 00:16:44,471
You'll show to the whole world how
those who pray at night...

146
00:16:44,471 --> 00:16:48,881
... can be fighters in the morning.

147
00:16:49,689 --> 00:16:54,739
Come on. Your horses shall be fast
and your weapons shall be sharp.

148
00:16:54,739 --> 00:16:56,569
As you order, my Sheikh.

149
00:17:18,183 --> 00:17:26,453
Cerkutay! Tell the Nökers.
No one will attack before I say a word.

150
00:17:27,007 --> 00:17:32,727
The Nökers in covers will stay in cover
no matter what.

151
00:17:32,929 --> 00:17:37,959
If they have to, they must
go back to cover.

152
00:17:39,396 --> 00:17:44,036
Don't kill Dündar.
That's for Osman to do.

153
00:17:47,432 --> 00:17:49,502
As you order, Balgay.

154
00:18:03,304 --> 00:18:07,304
Commander Balgay! Do you think
Osman is playing with us again?

155
00:18:08,211 --> 00:18:11,121
- He's nowhere to be seen.
- Don't worry.

156
00:18:12,256 --> 00:18:14,866
Osman is as crafty as a wolf.

157
00:18:15,350 --> 00:18:19,560
He knows that he can't deal
with Geyhatu without me.

158
00:18:21,171 --> 00:18:25,171
That's why he can't do wrong to me.

159
00:18:28,748 --> 00:18:32,338
I don't know why we're
involved in his fight with Alişar.

160
00:18:32,846 --> 00:18:37,516
Instead of him joining our fight,
we're swinging swords for him.

161
00:18:37,661 --> 00:18:41,241
Alişar isn't only fighting with Osman.

162
00:18:42,101 --> 00:18:47,041
He worked with Geyhatu and destroyed
all my plans.

163
00:18:47,714 --> 00:18:53,894
Geyhatu will be very angry if he finds out
that we worked with Osman to end Alişar.

164
00:18:55,090 --> 00:18:57,910
We'll take no prisoners.

165
00:18:59,467 --> 00:19:01,207
The dead can't talk.

166
00:19:02,523 --> 00:19:11,183
Osman will be responsible for this for
being in beef with Alişar.

167
00:19:13,992 --> 00:19:19,392
So Osman will feel Geyhatu's wrath.

168
00:19:19,897 --> 00:19:27,707
While they fight,
I'll destroy both of them.

169
00:19:29,246 --> 00:19:33,246
I'm behind you until the whole
world kneels before you, Commander Balgay.

170
00:19:34,134 --> 00:19:37,014
Bless your new position.

171
00:20:21,681 --> 00:20:27,641
My Bey. You were right.
The vulture is waiting to end us.

172
00:20:27,641 --> 00:20:31,601
- Dogs!
- As if he wasn't controlling Dündar Bey.

173
00:20:31,974 --> 00:20:35,404
He's throwing him into the fire.
Coward!

174
00:20:35,664 --> 00:20:40,184
My Bey! Alişar is ours.
Let's go and end him.

175
00:20:41,448 --> 00:20:47,688
Brother. The road to victory
is full of disorder.

176
00:20:48,511 --> 00:20:51,711
- Don't forget that.
- My Bey.

177
00:20:52,686 --> 00:20:55,556
I'm always honoured to fight with you.

178
00:20:55,866 --> 00:21:03,106
If I die, I'll die with gratitude towards
you and my Allah.

179
00:21:04,707 --> 00:21:08,207
Thank you, brother, thank you!

180
00:21:09,569 --> 00:21:16,469
This is our first revolt to the Mongols
and their supporters...

181
00:21:16,975 --> 00:21:20,835
... who settled on
the destroyed Seljuk throne.

182
00:21:22,038 --> 00:21:26,328
May Allah help us in this cause.

183
00:21:26,504 --> 00:21:28,794
- Amen!
- Amen!

184
00:21:32,588 --> 00:21:33,738
Let's go!

185
00:22:23,605 --> 00:22:26,575
Clouds of gloom are all over you again.

186
00:22:26,728 --> 00:22:29,848
I'm afraid of that cursed Osman, Aygül.

187
00:22:31,878 --> 00:22:37,228
I can't relax before your father
returns safe and sound.

188
00:22:38,398 --> 00:22:42,398
Don't worry.
Wait for Osman to stop breathing.

189
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:15,190
Burçin! You look worried.
What happened?

190
00:23:15,441 --> 00:23:18,191
Did something bad happen, my daughter?

191
00:23:18,306 --> 00:23:23,206
Demirci Bey's daughter visited.
Bala Hatun's dowries have arrived.

192
00:23:24,340 --> 00:23:27,460
They married with Osman, it seems.

193
00:23:29,127 --> 00:23:35,717
They're nowhere to be seen.
But everything is already at the Tent.

194
00:23:38,253 --> 00:23:41,123
All the Beys are in the caged tents.

195
00:23:41,482 --> 00:23:43,882
It is said that they'll be executed.

196
00:23:44,056 --> 00:23:45,536
My Allah...

197
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:50,820
May Allah almighty help our Beys.

198
00:23:52,757 --> 00:23:58,817
Osman...
May your tricks backfire on you!

199
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:02,550
While you're dreaming about
going to sleep with your wife...

200
00:24:02,550 --> 00:24:06,550
... you'll be hugging snakes
in deep pits, Osman.

201
00:24:07,229 --> 00:24:09,049
We're almost there.

202
00:26:29,238 --> 00:26:30,568
Where are you headed to?

203
00:26:30,568 --> 00:26:33,608
We're bringing fruits and vegetables
to Aygül Hatun's mansion.

204
00:27:10,677 --> 00:27:12,377
Fruits and vegetables.

205
00:28:09,140 --> 00:28:10,680
Alişar...

206
00:28:11,502 --> 00:28:13,272
You also came, huh?

207
00:28:59,254 --> 00:29:05,984
You don't have beef with me.
Too late for you to realise, Alişar!

208
00:29:09,228 --> 00:29:17,018
Cut his head, put it on a spear and
place is somewhere Osman Bey will see.

209
00:29:19,809 --> 00:29:25,249
I promised you victory and victory only.

210
00:29:25,546 --> 00:29:28,646
What awaits those who support Balgay,
you say?

211
00:29:28,646 --> 00:29:32,286
Wealth! Fame!

212
00:29:32,595 --> 00:29:40,525
- Balgay!
- Balgay!

213
00:29:46,100 --> 00:29:47,380
Balgay!

214
00:29:53,006 --> 00:29:54,466
Ambush!

215
00:30:06,084 --> 00:30:07,154
Balgay!

216
00:30:15,475 --> 00:30:18,405
I brought you death!

217
00:30:20,507 --> 00:30:24,137
I brought you death, Balgay!
Death!

218
00:31:19,226 --> 00:31:22,846
Ambush! Take Cover!
Archers! What are you waiting for?

219
00:31:31,243 --> 00:31:33,053
Swords up!

220
00:31:38,193 --> 00:31:42,663
- Let's go!
- In the name of Allah!

221
00:31:48,572 --> 00:31:50,962
Ya Allah!

222
00:31:51,484 --> 00:31:53,544
Come to your death, Osman.

223
00:33:53,437 --> 00:33:54,937
Alişar!

224
00:33:55,823 --> 00:33:59,423
Get out of the place you're hiding in!
Come on!

225
00:34:20,673 --> 00:34:23,670
Here I am.

226
00:34:25,881 --> 00:34:31,391
The most powerful will be victorious!

227
00:34:37,490 --> 00:34:39,010
Come here!

228
00:34:40,194 --> 00:34:42,104
Attack, valiants!

229
00:35:15,600 --> 00:35:19,600
Böke! I need Osman alive.

230
00:35:45,270 --> 00:35:49,270
- They're getting suspicious, Bala.
- Our wedding feast is ready then.

231
00:36:03,589 --> 00:36:07,019
Aygül Hatun has no such orders.
go back.

232
00:36:07,019 --> 00:36:11,349
How can that be? Adelfosmo!
Give him the documents.

233
00:36:16,815 --> 00:36:21,255
In the name of Allah!

234
00:36:23,109 --> 00:36:25,619
- Ambush!
- There's an ambush!

235
00:36:35,264 --> 00:36:40,514
May blood rain upon the degenerates!

236
00:36:40,698 --> 00:36:41,928
Ya Allah!

237
00:36:49,005 --> 00:36:51,985
- This way!
- Run!

238
00:36:52,608 --> 00:36:56,958
- Ambush!
- They're looking for trouble!

239
00:36:57,522 --> 00:37:00,312
They went too far
by attacking the mansion!

240
00:37:00,312 --> 00:37:03,962
Come on! Go, soldiers!
Run!

241
00:37:03,962 --> 00:37:06,542
They're here. So they were
planning for this!

242
00:37:06,542 --> 00:37:12,232
You! Look at me! Tell everyone inside to
close their windows and take their swords!

243
00:37:21,201 --> 00:37:23,261
Ya Allah!

244
00:37:30,902 --> 00:37:36,052
Karapolat! Get your steel sword up!
Allahu Akbar!

245
00:37:37,254 --> 00:37:42,304
Hit then, valiants!
For the babies and martyrs!

246
00:37:42,586 --> 00:37:44,866
Allahu Akbar!

247
00:38:15,563 --> 00:38:19,743
Close the windows and cages!
Quick! Let's go!

248
00:38:21,062 --> 00:38:26,562
This is the Bannerlord's mansion!
If Alişar Bey isn't here, his Hatun is!

249
00:38:26,868 --> 00:38:29,878
Don't let them through!

250
00:38:29,947 --> 00:38:35,667
I'd rather die than be captured by them!
Let's go, soldiers!

251
00:38:35,943 --> 00:38:41,643
Run, soldiers! Quick!
Come on!

252
00:38:56,121 --> 00:38:58,511
Go! Never surrender!

253
00:39:02,066 --> 00:39:05,736
Surround the place!
Don't let them get us in the back.

254
00:39:05,806 --> 00:39:07,256
Let's go!

255
00:39:19,349 --> 00:39:22,269
Go downstairs! Come on!

256
00:39:22,269 --> 00:39:25,329
We won't surrender!
We won't resign either!

257
00:39:26,945 --> 00:39:28,355
Bring it on!

258
00:39:44,582 --> 00:39:46,452
He is out of arrows.

259
00:39:47,655 --> 00:39:49,685
Let me deal with Balgay.

260
00:40:17,974 --> 00:40:25,444
When did you forget the days you crawled
to my presence for help, Dündar?

261
00:40:25,738 --> 00:40:29,018
Yesterdays are over, Balgay.

262
00:40:29,180 --> 00:40:31,940
Now you're mine!

263
00:40:38,419 --> 00:40:43,509
Fool Dündar! Even your wife Zöhre
is smarter than you.

264
00:40:44,673 --> 00:40:47,103
She knew who to ask help from.

265
00:40:47,798 --> 00:40:49,418
You'll die!

266
00:40:49,765 --> 00:40:54,895
I'll make a drum from your skin
and play it in Kayı Tent!

267
00:40:56,553 --> 00:41:03,153
Do you think I'm like the young Osman
you're working with?

268
00:41:13,472 --> 00:41:16,902
Maybe I'll ascent to heaven from here.

269
00:41:17,895 --> 00:41:22,585
But I'll take you with me.

270
00:41:25,722 --> 00:41:32,212
Balgay! Come here.
Come here and taste my sword!

271
00:41:32,212 --> 00:41:33,602
Come here!

272
00:42:43,920 --> 00:42:45,410
Cerkutay!

273
00:42:46,233 --> 00:42:49,183
You take Balgay out of here.
I'll deal with them.

274
00:42:54,652 --> 00:42:59,902
Young Osman...
Young, mad Osman...

275
00:43:01,606 --> 00:43:04,696
Osman who opposes the state...

276
00:43:06,708 --> 00:43:11,248
You're in the Bannerlord
Alişar Bey's arms.

277
00:43:19,157 --> 00:43:21,297
Now, your end is certain.

278
00:43:22,281 --> 00:43:26,281
I've come to take the Mongol's
leash from your neck, Alişar.

279
00:43:28,525 --> 00:43:34,365
You'll get your freedom
after I take your life.

280
00:43:37,788 --> 00:43:44,048
You talk too much
but you're too dumb, Osman.

281
00:43:46,355 --> 00:43:51,835
I'll torture you until you
beg me to stop like a dog!

282
00:43:59,147 --> 00:44:03,147
In the name of Allah...

283
00:44:04,144 --> 00:44:07,974
Attack, valiants!

284
00:44:29,905 --> 00:44:34,465
If Alişar finds out that Böke is lying,
then what will we do, my Bey?

285
00:44:34,465 --> 00:44:37,495
If you turn your back to the enemy,
you'll lose the war, Boran.

286
00:44:38,256 --> 00:44:42,066
Böke is an enemy,
just like Alişar and Balgay.

287
00:44:42,539 --> 00:44:44,279
We'll be cautious.

288
00:44:45,181 --> 00:44:48,781
I can't push my valiants into a war
by trusting Geyhatu's dog Böke.

289
00:44:56,877 --> 00:44:59,597
Ambush within ambush, Böke!

290
00:45:22,359 --> 00:45:24,049
Alişar is running away, my Bey!

291
00:45:24,578 --> 00:45:27,128
Böke! You go that way!

292
00:45:28,427 --> 00:45:30,637
Alişar!

293
00:47:09,260 --> 00:47:10,680
Come at me!

294
00:47:31,180 --> 00:47:34,290
Kill them all!
All of them!

295
00:49:33,916 --> 00:49:36,856
The oppression is over, my Gündüz!
It's over!

296
00:49:36,856 --> 00:49:38,986
It's over, Bamsı Bey! Over!

297
00:49:39,402 --> 00:49:46,662
I'll sacrifice countless goats after
I see this place burn to the ground!

298
00:49:46,772 --> 00:49:48,002
Hopefully!

299
00:49:49,215 --> 00:49:53,265
I'll sacrifice goats! Come on, valiants!
Break this door!

300
00:49:53,265 --> 00:49:57,025
- Let's do it!
- Come on!

301
00:50:03,920 --> 00:50:05,270
Come on!

302
00:50:08,092 --> 00:50:09,562
Come on!

303
00:50:17,460 --> 00:50:22,590
Come on, valiants!
For my Aybars! For our martyrs!

304
00:50:22,741 --> 00:50:24,131
Come on!

305
00:50:50,331 --> 00:50:53,970
Aygül Hatun! We can't hold much longer!
Escape! Save yourself!

306
00:50:53,970 --> 00:50:55,010
Shut up!

307
00:51:05,536 --> 00:51:07,906
- We can't deal with them, Aygül!
- Aygül!

308
00:51:07,906 --> 00:51:11,406
- We can't waste our lives!
- Let's go!

309
00:51:11,547 --> 00:51:13,627
No one leaves!

310
00:51:15,245 --> 00:51:16,795
Come on, valiants!

311
00:51:18,420 --> 00:51:21,580
For our martyrs!
Allahu Akbar!

312
00:51:21,580 --> 00:51:27,100
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

313
00:51:39,537 --> 00:51:43,927
Let's go, I say!
We'll deal with them tomorrow, let's go!

314
00:51:45,818 --> 00:51:50,058
It's a catch if I can get one of them!
Everyone will stay here!

315
00:51:50,500 --> 00:51:53,550
We won't let them get the mansion!

316
00:51:53,683 --> 00:51:56,813
We're surrounded!
Where will we escape from?

317
00:51:56,813 --> 00:51:58,433
How will we get out of here?

318
00:51:58,433 --> 00:52:01,203
There's a secret passage!
It leads outside.

319
00:52:01,803 --> 00:52:05,313
We'll get to safety without
anyone seeing us. Come on, Aygül!

320
00:52:15,871 --> 00:52:18,951
Valiants! Take the battering ram!

321
00:52:20,387 --> 00:52:21,517
Come on!

322
00:52:30,784 --> 00:52:32,524
Come on!
Allahu Akbar!

323
00:53:04,675 --> 00:53:07,075
Come on, valiants!
Come on!

324
00:53:21,030 --> 00:53:22,570
Allahu Akbar!

325
00:53:23,610 --> 00:53:25,550
In the name of Allah!

326
00:53:56,944 --> 00:53:58,834
Where is Zöhre Hatun?

327
00:54:00,849 --> 00:54:02,669
They escaped from the secret passage.

328
00:54:07,110 --> 00:54:08,410
Selcan Yenge?

329
00:54:08,410 --> 00:54:11,420
I couldn't sit while all
this fight was happening.

330
00:54:11,771 --> 00:54:14,321
I have a score to settle with Zöhre.

331
00:54:15,329 --> 00:54:17,179
I'll go after them.

332
00:54:18,126 --> 00:54:20,536
- Let's go! Move!
- Move!

333
00:54:56,411 --> 00:54:59,571
Osman won't stop following us.
Cut him off!

334
00:55:17,027 --> 00:55:21,125
Come now, Osman.
Geyhatu won't kill you...

335
00:55:21,624 --> 00:55:23,423
...I will.

336
00:55:34,100 --> 00:55:35,571
Useless fool!

337
00:56:00,546 --> 00:56:01,336
Father!

338
00:56:02,046 --> 00:56:03,570
Won't we go after Balgay?

339
00:56:04,024 --> 00:56:06,159
Do you think I care about Balgay?

340
00:56:07,129 --> 00:56:09,313
Let Alişar's men go after him.

341
00:56:10,291 --> 00:56:11,905
Osman is unpredictable.

342
00:56:12,078 --> 00:56:14,303
We shouldn't leave Alişar alone.

343
00:56:14,534 --> 00:56:17,660
I told you to stay calm but...
...I'm confused as well.

344
00:56:18,415 --> 00:56:20,575
He goes after Osman but sends
us here.

345
00:56:21,330 --> 00:56:23,808
And ever since the thing with
Melik, I'm disturbed.

346
00:56:25,471 --> 00:56:26,988
What if Osman is right?

347
00:56:28,273 --> 00:56:30,360
What if it was Alişar who killed
my brother?

348
00:56:33,630 --> 00:56:38,065
Then, I will take such a revenge that...

349
00:56:39,073 --> 00:56:40,956
...all the world will hear it!

350
00:56:41,101 --> 00:56:44,790
If it is true, then it will be us
who the world will be talking about.

351
00:56:45,961 --> 00:56:48,327
What about my sister?

352
00:56:48,863 --> 00:56:51,441
Huh, father?
What about my sister?

353
00:56:51,479 --> 00:56:54,666
How will she recover from the shame of
being in the same bed with...

354
00:56:54,666 --> 00:56:56,086
...the killer of her brother!

355
00:57:01,744 --> 00:57:04,401
We need to go to the encampment.

356
00:57:05,273 --> 00:57:07,072
They are waiting for us.

357
00:57:09,199 --> 00:57:10,212
Move.

358
00:57:35,238 --> 00:57:36,103
Move.

359
00:57:37,297 --> 00:57:38,548
Hurry.

360
00:58:02,042 --> 00:58:03,274
Here...

361
00:58:03,772 --> 00:58:04,953
...I'm in front of you!

362
00:58:07,950 --> 00:58:09,001
Come on...

363
00:58:10,291 --> 00:58:11,403
...let's finish it.

364
00:58:12,112 --> 00:58:14,731
But a sword raised against me...

365
00:58:16,100 --> 00:58:17,628
...is raised against the state.

366
00:58:18,514 --> 00:58:21,815
Sheathe your weapon while you have
a chance.

367
00:58:22,106 --> 00:58:23,361
Let us reach an agreement.

368
00:58:23,693 --> 00:58:26,891
The state of yours which steps
on the Laws of Turks shall be ruined!

369
00:58:27,210 --> 00:58:28,925
May you lay under its ruins, Alişar!

370
00:58:29,555 --> 00:58:32,344
From now, your state is no more...

371
00:58:32,761 --> 00:58:35,248
...both to me and to Turks.

372
00:58:36,052 --> 00:58:37,638
What will you do?

373
00:58:38,848 --> 00:58:41,063
Will you have khutbahs in your name?

374
00:58:41,497 --> 00:58:43,265
Will you make your own coin?

375
00:58:44,728 --> 00:58:47,230
Young boy...
Mad boy...

376
00:58:48,358 --> 00:58:52,246
Where you and your lineage will
end up is...

377
00:58:52,745 --> 00:58:56,152
... graves without al-fatehah!

378
00:58:56,456 --> 00:58:59,519
They will read al-Fatihah for us,
even after thousands of years.

379
00:58:59,869 --> 00:59:03,237
But you will only be remembered
by shame!

380
00:59:07,392 --> 00:59:09,601
Die, then.

381
00:59:17,024 --> 00:59:18,206
Alişar...

382
00:59:24,998 --> 00:59:27,815
What is it?
Are you going to kill me?

383
00:59:28,367 --> 00:59:30,714
C'mon, do it!

384
00:59:31,894 --> 00:59:34,125
There is no easy death for you,
Alişar!

385
00:59:34,992 --> 00:59:37,447
You took my honor, my position...

386
00:59:38,188 --> 00:59:40,109
...everything I had!

387
00:59:41,172 --> 00:59:44,511
What are you waiting for?
Kill me!

388
00:59:44,511 --> 00:59:47,378
Poke my eyes out, skin me alive...

389
00:59:47,921 --> 00:59:51,833
...let my blood run over my body!

390
00:59:53,921 --> 00:59:58,434
What you say fits the Mongols which
you're a slave of.

391
01:00:00,473 --> 01:00:05,089
In these lands which my father conquered..

392
01:00:05,559 --> 01:00:09,958
...I will put you in a grave but no one
will know where it is.

393
01:02:10,195 --> 01:02:14,524
Mashallah!

394
01:02:20,337 --> 01:02:22,980
This flag has been the symbol
of justice...

395
01:02:23,718 --> 01:02:25,973
...rights and laws.

396
01:02:28,820 --> 01:02:31,383
May the light it gives...

397
01:02:31,730 --> 01:02:33,224
...illuminate the whole world.

398
01:02:35,248 --> 01:02:38,171
The bow frightens tyrants...

399
01:02:38,819 --> 01:02:40,067
...the arrows...

400
01:02:40,674 --> 01:02:42,472
...gives hope to the innocent.

401
01:02:43,036 --> 01:02:44,788
May the shadow of this flag...

402
01:02:45,682 --> 01:02:47,320
...be a shelter for...

403
01:02:47,844 --> 01:02:49,082
...all the poor!

404
01:03:31,157 --> 01:03:33,268
Mother, they went this way.

405
01:03:56,660 --> 01:03:57,566
Aygül.

406
01:03:58,275 --> 01:04:01,173
-What are you waiting for? Move.
-Go, mother.

407
01:04:01,286 --> 01:04:02,858
They must be after us.

408
01:04:04,509 --> 01:04:07,129
If I don't remove the tracks we will
all be captured.

409
01:04:08,081 --> 01:04:09,683
Let Burçin go...

410
01:04:10,851 --> 01:04:12,675
...and stay with me.

411
01:04:12,816 --> 01:04:14,958
Do as I say, mother.
I will find you later.

412
01:04:15,698 --> 01:04:17,646
Don't look behind.
Move.

413
01:04:19,215 --> 01:04:20,535
Aygül.

414
01:05:04,937 --> 01:05:06,418
They came here.

415
01:05:11,521 --> 01:05:12,835
Tracks show this way.

416
01:05:23,500 --> 01:05:26,191
It's still fresh.
We should follow.

417
01:06:05,484 --> 01:06:07,231
Are you looking for us, Dündar Bey?

418
01:06:17,457 --> 01:06:19,048
So...

419
01:06:19,733 --> 01:06:21,384
...so, it was a trap.

420
01:06:26,630 --> 01:06:29,191
I won't let you take my
father while I'm still alive.

421
01:06:30,390 --> 01:06:32,189
You will kill me first!

422
01:06:33,186 --> 01:06:37,887
And I won't let my son be a
cover for me.

423
01:06:39,021 --> 01:06:41,126
Either you will kill us...

424
01:06:42,440 --> 01:06:45,370
...or we will kill you.

425
01:06:45,488 --> 01:06:47,287
Come on!
Come on!

426
01:06:52,811 --> 01:06:55,144
We didn't come here to fight,
Dündar Bey.

427
01:07:03,894 --> 01:07:05,977
We didn't come here to fight.

428
01:07:13,860 --> 01:07:17,202
What is this gibberish?
Speak!

429
01:07:21,806 --> 01:07:24,399
You are too blinded to see the truth,
Dündar Bey.

430
01:07:26,219 --> 01:07:27,343
We need you alive.

431
01:07:27,462 --> 01:07:29,357
Not dead.

432
01:08:12,783 --> 01:08:17,513
Böke! Kill him!
Kill him!

433
01:08:18,496 --> 01:08:22,916
When I was about to kill you,
you said that I was wrong.

434
01:08:24,557 --> 01:08:27,511
Let's see who is wrong now.

435
01:08:46,905 --> 01:08:49,353
That is for another day, Böke.

436
01:10:54,628 --> 01:10:56,798
You came to my house!

437
01:10:57,816 --> 01:10:58,975
Shame!

438
01:11:03,879 --> 01:11:06,781
Lower your weapon, Aygül.
I don't want to see you bleed.

439
01:11:26,458 --> 01:11:28,617
You thought I ran away!

440
01:11:29,852 --> 01:11:32,674
But I don't run away.
Especially not from you!

441
01:11:49,495 --> 01:11:52,199
From now you don't have me.

442
01:11:52,667 --> 01:11:55,318
If you make another move,
you will die.

443
01:11:57,461 --> 01:12:00,847
You spoke truly. I never had you.

444
01:12:02,755 --> 01:12:06,009
You are a clapper for those who
step on our laws...

445
01:12:06,009 --> 01:12:08,690
...and a nebbish that helps
those who think they are a Bey..

446
01:12:08,690 --> 01:12:09,870
...by killing a Bey.

447
01:12:34,763 --> 01:12:35,667
Look.

448
01:12:37,453 --> 01:12:39,122
Do you see?

449
01:12:40,958 --> 01:12:45,906
They did everything they could...

450
01:12:45,906 --> 01:12:48,128
...and took the throne my father...

451
01:12:48,159 --> 01:12:50,028
...who is the real Bey.

452
01:12:51,118 --> 01:12:54,238
Now they are bloodthirsty because
he wanted his right.

453
01:13:01,244 --> 01:13:04,619
These are people who give up
on their own lives for a throne.

454
01:13:07,139 --> 01:13:09,151
Speak! Who are you?

455
01:13:12,182 --> 01:13:15,351
That Osman who made you fly
high in love...

456
01:13:18,260 --> 01:13:20,488
...will let you down, too.

457
01:13:23,537 --> 01:13:27,712
When you stand against him,
he will do the same to you.

458
01:13:32,741 --> 01:13:34,733
Don't get happy that
you are a bride now.

459
01:13:36,185 --> 01:13:38,327
Wait, Bala Hatun.

460
01:13:43,173 --> 01:13:44,472
He is my Bey.

461
01:13:45,194 --> 01:13:46,754
He knows the best.

462
01:13:47,580 --> 01:13:49,740
You should think more about...

463
01:13:50,396 --> 01:13:51,964
...what will you do now.

464
01:14:14,665 --> 01:14:16,381
No...
No...

465
01:14:17,138 --> 01:14:18,701
No, I can't...

466
01:14:19,570 --> 01:14:21,788
I can't leave Aygül alone.
I will go back.

467
01:14:22,305 --> 01:14:25,021
Don't, Zöhre Hatun.
We can't handle them.

468
01:14:25,766 --> 01:14:27,280
They won't hurt Aygül.

469
01:14:27,799 --> 01:14:29,305
But they will kill us.

470
01:14:31,984 --> 01:14:35,088
You leave and save your life.
I can't leave my daughter alone.

471
01:15:10,771 --> 01:15:14,605
Dündar Bey and Bahadır entrapped
Balgay.

472
01:15:20,240 --> 01:15:23,152
From now, you are alone, Osman.

473
01:15:25,081 --> 01:15:26,942
They both are captured.

474
01:15:28,425 --> 01:15:31,254
They are on their way.
My warriors will bring them here.

475
01:15:33,559 --> 01:15:36,507
They will face justice just like
you will.

476
01:15:41,133 --> 01:15:43,029
And about Gündüz Bey
and Bamsı Bey...

477
01:15:45,058 --> 01:15:47,795
They went to your mansion...

478
01:15:48,566 --> 01:15:50,799
...which is more unholy
than Byzantine palace.

479
01:15:52,796 --> 01:15:55,742
From now, both your mansion...

480
01:15:56,045 --> 01:15:58,093
...and your flag is on my hands!

481
01:15:59,463 --> 01:16:02,796
You are nothing, Alişar.

482
01:16:03,336 --> 01:16:04,572
Nothing.

483
01:16:08,566 --> 01:16:11,439
Prepare your horse...

484
01:16:12,176 --> 01:16:14,246
...to take that dog away.

485
01:16:17,184 --> 01:16:19,487
- Yes, my Bey.
- Move.

486
01:16:29,778 --> 01:16:34,680
You were a dog to Geyhatu who wanted
to overthrow the emperor of Byzantine.!

487
01:16:35,667 --> 01:16:38,467
You caused the deaths of many people
from your blood.

488
01:16:39,469 --> 01:16:43,498
Now...
It's time to pay, Alişar.

489
01:16:47,507 --> 01:16:49,986
Osman...
Osman...

490
01:16:52,148 --> 01:16:54,302
Statecraft, Osman.

491
01:16:56,774 --> 01:17:00,638
It is nothing like the mind of a shepherd.

492
01:17:03,978 --> 01:17:07,026
Such a shepherd that...

493
01:17:08,698 --> 01:17:11,452
... he stopped all your plans
with Geyhatu.

494
01:17:13,439 --> 01:17:15,772
Sofia became the Emperor's prisoner.

495
01:17:20,262 --> 01:17:24,824
We went to the Emperor and gave the names
of the Monks of Margareth.

496
01:17:30,661 --> 01:17:33,647
Your uncle...
Sungurtekin...

497
01:17:42,736 --> 01:17:46,317
He was in this from the beginning.

498
01:17:48,804 --> 01:17:51,752
Be afraid of Geyhatu's wrath, Osman.

499
01:18:08,460 --> 01:18:10,460
What kind of a devil are you?

500
01:18:12,908 --> 01:18:15,066
First, you killed Batur.

501
01:18:16,723 --> 01:18:19,059
Then, you married Aygül.

502
01:18:22,087 --> 01:18:24,342
You caused a civil war.

503
01:18:28,685 --> 01:18:31,990
Am I the devil?

504
01:18:32,595 --> 01:18:33,988
Or is it Dündar?

505
01:18:36,939 --> 01:18:41,318
An ambitious fool who set his eyes
on the throne of your sick father.

506
01:18:43,715 --> 01:18:48,681
With few words, he saw you as a rival on
his way to the throne...

507
01:18:49,492 --> 01:18:51,448
...and he became your enemy.

508
01:18:53,244 --> 01:18:55,495
He didn't doubt that you killed
his son.

509
01:18:57,261 --> 01:19:00,430
Nor did he doubt about giving
his daughter to me.

510
01:19:04,925 --> 01:19:09,816
If you are looking for a devil,
look among you, Osman.

511
01:19:11,651 --> 01:19:14,292
Among those who come after...

512
01:19:14,838 --> 01:19:16,671
...your grandfather Süleyman Shah.

513
01:19:17,979 --> 01:19:19,286
Alişar!

514
01:19:21,765 --> 01:19:22,635
Fool.

515
01:19:25,183 --> 01:19:26,574
Alişar!

516
01:19:31,674 --> 01:19:33,816
Alişar!
Alişar!

517
01:19:35,241 --> 01:19:37,254
Alişar!
Alişar!

518
01:19:43,421 --> 01:19:46,652
Control your anger, uncle!

519
01:19:53,893 --> 01:19:55,603
You are late, uncle!

520
01:19:57,046 --> 01:19:58,592
You are late!

521
01:20:13,299 --> 01:20:14,522
Batur...

522
01:20:19,030 --> 01:20:22,245
Osman... Osman, I...

523
01:20:22,593 --> 01:20:26,048
What have I done?
What have I done?

524
01:20:29,497 --> 01:20:32,094
Batur...
My son...

525
01:20:35,183 --> 01:20:37,276
Uncle...

526
01:20:46,984 --> 01:20:48,892
Uncle, uncle!

527
01:20:49,562 --> 01:20:51,554
Uncle. Uncle!
Get up!

528
01:21:08,321 --> 01:21:09,923
My boy...

529
01:21:10,875 --> 01:21:12,869
My Batur...

530
01:21:22,362 --> 01:21:23,610
Alişar...

531
01:21:28,673 --> 01:21:31,330
Hang on, just a little bit more.

532
01:21:32,415 --> 01:21:33,724
Selcan Hatun!

533
01:21:38,945 --> 01:21:40,697
Let my daughter go.

534
01:21:45,749 --> 01:21:47,937
Let us part our ways without blood.

535
01:21:48,750 --> 01:21:50,499
So, you don't want blood, huh?

536
01:21:52,459 --> 01:21:54,874
She has a golden heart.

537
01:21:56,956 --> 01:21:58,780
If is that so...

538
01:21:59,597 --> 01:22:01,261
...come and get your daughter.

539
01:22:03,595 --> 01:22:05,685
I say let Aygül go.

540
01:22:05,770 --> 01:22:08,073
Confronting the Bannerlord does
not benefit you.

541
01:22:09,277 --> 01:22:14,685
By thinking of benefits, you gave your
daughter away.

542
01:22:16,437 --> 01:22:19,331
I don't need any benefits.

543
01:22:19,481 --> 01:22:22,191
If you didn't go mad about the throne...

544
01:22:23,318 --> 01:22:27,356
...that banner lord would help the
whole family...

545
01:22:27,755 --> 01:22:29,746
...and the tent.

546
01:22:30,573 --> 01:22:35,022
But everything happened because of your
ambition.

547
01:22:38,556 --> 01:22:40,034
Alişar...

548
01:22:41,864 --> 01:22:44,409
How did you do that to my son...

549
01:22:45,635 --> 01:22:47,740
...to my daughter...

550
01:22:50,105 --> 01:22:52,964
What kind of a conscience is this?

551
01:22:54,191 --> 01:22:55,319
What kind of?

552
01:22:57,394 --> 01:22:58,693
What kind of?

553
01:23:00,604 --> 01:23:02,668
You gave a son for the tent.

554
01:23:03,585 --> 01:23:06,597
Wasn't it you who said that...

555
01:23:07,050 --> 01:23:11,099
...I'd give a thousand son
to my tents.

556
01:23:14,096 --> 01:23:15,399
Huh?

557
01:23:18,306 --> 01:23:19,235
Uncle.

558
01:23:22,348 --> 01:23:23,163
Uncle!

559
01:23:24,143 --> 01:23:24,962
Uncle.

560
01:23:27,573 --> 01:23:28,381
Uncle!

561
01:23:37,752 --> 01:23:42,744
I had the killer of my son marry
my daughter.

562
01:23:56,617 --> 01:23:57,763
Osman...

563
01:23:59,429 --> 01:24:03,382
...my nephew, forgive me.

564
01:24:09,772 --> 01:24:11,720
I was a victim of my ambition.

565
01:24:12,988 --> 01:24:17,018
But don't spare my life.

566
01:24:19,393 --> 01:24:21,907
Forgive my Bahadır.

567
01:24:22,306 --> 01:24:25,840
I took him to this path...

568
01:24:29,569 --> 01:24:30,906
Forgive him.

569
01:24:50,541 --> 01:24:54,723
Now swing this black weapon of yours...

570
01:24:55,932 --> 01:24:57,895
...onto my neck.

571
01:24:59,849 --> 01:25:01,612
Behead me.

572
01:25:02,945 --> 01:25:05,391
Finish me.

573
01:25:07,887 --> 01:25:09,329
Osman...

574
01:25:10,544 --> 01:25:14,122
...don't let me live with this shame.

575
01:25:21,592 --> 01:25:25,762
Because of my ambition and stupidity...

576
01:25:26,038 --> 01:25:30,805
...I have the blood of my child on
my hands...

577
01:25:32,266 --> 01:25:35,908
...dignity of my girl...

578
01:25:54,480 --> 01:25:57,155
How can I look Aygül on the face?

579
01:25:58,409 --> 01:26:01,100
I ruined the lives of...

580
01:26:02,031 --> 01:26:03,988
...both my children.

581
01:26:04,897 --> 01:26:06,342
Come on, Osman.

582
01:26:07,217 --> 01:26:11,204
I don't deserve to live.
Take my life.

583
01:26:14,174 --> 01:26:15,612
Come on.

584
01:26:16,088 --> 01:26:16,973
Come on.

585
01:26:42,882 --> 01:26:44,116
Uncle...

586
01:26:46,330 --> 01:26:48,560
...the decision about you...

587
01:26:49,861 --> 01:26:52,093
...will be made by my father.

588
01:26:53,547 --> 01:26:55,249
But...

589
01:27:01,226 --> 01:27:03,845
...you will get what you deserve.

590
01:27:11,452 --> 01:27:13,614
We wanted to be united.

591
01:27:13,614 --> 01:27:16,615
To face the difficulties together.

592
01:27:17,028 --> 01:27:18,755
But we couldn't convince you.

593
01:27:19,093 --> 01:27:22,160
It turned out that you are not the one.

594
01:27:24,528 --> 01:27:27,771
Whatever I can say to you, it is not
enough, Zöhre.

595
01:27:31,219 --> 01:27:33,018
Do you know what they say?

596
01:27:36,782 --> 01:27:42,114
'Ignoble' that's exactly what you are.

597
01:28:19,496 --> 01:28:21,050
Murderers.

598
01:28:22,754 --> 01:28:24,456
Murderers.

599
01:28:26,268 --> 01:28:27,636
Murderers!

600
01:28:29,257 --> 01:28:30,751
Murderers!

601
01:28:33,050 --> 01:28:34,610
Murderers!

602
01:29:12,491 --> 01:29:13,504
Balgay.

603
01:29:13,773 --> 01:29:14,889
Balgay.

604
01:29:16,917 --> 01:29:24,477
Haven't I told you that warriors on cover
will not leave their position no matter what!

605
01:29:28,304 --> 01:29:30,477
Kongar was leading them.
It's his fault.

606
01:29:30,570 --> 01:29:33,556
Enough! If it wasn't for Kongar...

607
01:29:33,971 --> 01:29:35,756
...you would be dead.

608
01:29:38,736 --> 01:29:40,458
You are bleeding too much.

609
01:29:41,002 --> 01:29:42,373
We need to brand it.

610
01:29:42,929 --> 01:29:45,290
Kongar will find our tracks anyway.

611
01:29:47,120 --> 01:29:47,944
Come on.

612
01:30:44,020 --> 01:30:44,867
Osman.

613
01:30:52,726 --> 01:30:53,468
Balgay.

614
01:30:55,397 --> 01:30:57,806
-Are you alright?
-You sold me out, Osman.

615
01:30:58,573 --> 01:31:00,475
I was going to die because of you.

616
01:31:04,622 --> 01:31:06,770
We need to take this arrow out.

617
01:31:08,377 --> 01:31:10,188
What are you waiting for, Cerkutay?

618
01:31:13,927 --> 01:31:18,732
First, you ambushed us.
And now you are trying to help, huh?

619
01:31:20,308 --> 01:31:24,041
I don't need anyone's help!

620
01:31:25,681 --> 01:31:27,345
I didn't set the ambush.

621
01:31:29,476 --> 01:31:31,807
It was Böke who you trusted much.

622
01:31:33,153 --> 01:31:35,624
He sold us both out.

623
01:31:36,255 --> 01:31:37,975
But...

624
01:31:39,968 --> 01:31:41,378
...don't worry.

625
01:31:42,735 --> 01:31:44,507
I killed him.

626
01:31:47,580 --> 01:31:50,368
Who betrayed isn't important.

627
01:31:52,232 --> 01:31:54,650
My Nökers were slaughtered.

628
01:31:55,407 --> 01:31:57,722
And my condition is...

629
01:31:58,358 --> 01:32:00,446
From now on, we'll do as I say.

630
01:32:07,119 --> 01:32:08,843
I got what I wanted, Balgay.

631
01:32:11,112 --> 01:32:12,746
But...

632
01:32:13,808 --> 01:32:15,726
...I will still keep my word to you.

633
01:32:20,876 --> 01:32:23,379
On your battle...

634
01:32:24,336 --> 01:32:26,477
...I will help you kill Geyhatu.

635
01:32:29,765 --> 01:32:30,560
But...

636
01:32:31,110 --> 01:32:34,965
...if the Noyans you will bring are
like Böke...

637
01:32:35,940 --> 01:32:38,964
...this time it will be me who will
kill you.

638
01:32:39,737 --> 01:32:45,540
When I return, everything will be
different.

639
01:32:48,699 --> 01:32:51,389
Now you got what you wanted.

640
01:32:52,196 --> 01:32:55,267
Now you are in my debt.

641
01:32:56,330 --> 01:32:58,584
A valiant one doesn't forget
his debt.

642
01:33:00,430 --> 01:33:03,280
I don't forget anything.

643
01:33:05,264 --> 01:33:09,629
Don't die until we get even.

644
01:33:44,395 --> 01:33:46,606
Those Nökers on the cover...

645
01:33:47,979 --> 01:33:50,661
...I ordered them to stay.

646
01:33:53,020 --> 01:33:55,148
You will answer for this.

647
01:33:55,179 --> 01:33:57,872
Kongar was leading them, Kongar.

648
01:34:33,551 --> 01:34:36,667
-Selcan Hatun.
-You got her.

649
01:34:36,793 --> 01:34:38,517
We did, Gündüz.

650
01:34:38,517 --> 01:34:43,916
I will see you later.
You will answer for capturing...

651
01:34:44,133 --> 01:34:46,676
...the real Hatun of Kayı.

652
01:34:48,157 --> 01:34:49,590
Bamsı Bey...

653
01:34:53,878 --> 01:34:55,794
Don't listen to her.

654
01:34:58,442 --> 01:35:01,221
Who are you to listen to us.

655
01:35:04,461 --> 01:35:08,951
The only thing you know is using a weapon
and overthrowing a Bey.

656
01:35:14,462 --> 01:35:15,357
Come on.

657
01:35:15,357 --> 01:35:18,165
Take them away. Come on.

658
01:35:43,351 --> 01:35:45,069
They ambushed us.

659
01:35:45,450 --> 01:35:48,036
She tried to kill Bala.
She got wounded in the fight.

660
01:35:49,738 --> 01:35:53,959
Burçin... Burçin, my girl.
You will be fine.

661
01:35:54,127 --> 01:36:00,338
Burçin, you will be fine.
I promised to your father.

662
01:36:00,890 --> 01:36:05,209
Who did you side with, Burçin?

663
01:36:05,361 --> 01:36:08,957
How did you end up with
these snakes?

664
01:36:10,364 --> 01:36:15,890
Take her to the doctor right away.
She needs to be tended.

665
01:36:15,890 --> 01:36:17,722
Hurry, hurry!

666
01:36:21,753 --> 01:36:27,140
Gonca Hatun, you are wounded, too.
Go with them. Take her to the doctor.

667
01:36:29,675 --> 01:36:32,506
-Go, go.
-Bamsı Bey.

668
01:36:34,669 --> 01:36:36,277
She is severely wounded.

669
01:36:36,603 --> 01:36:38,180
She lost too much blood.

670
01:36:38,369 --> 01:36:41,191
You should know.
May Allah help her.

671
01:37:11,000 --> 01:37:13,027
You are victorious, Osman Bey.

672
01:37:13,884 --> 01:37:16,928
We are just followers of Allah, Göktuğ.

673
01:37:17,591 --> 01:37:19,229
Allah is victorious.

674
01:37:21,597 --> 01:37:24,545
I was with Balgay.
His wound is deep.

675
01:37:25,193 --> 01:37:26,794
But that wound won't kill him.

676
01:37:28,067 --> 01:37:29,607
They are waiting for you.

677
01:37:29,893 --> 01:37:33,188
No, Osman Bey, no.
There is no easy death for him.

678
01:37:33,759 --> 01:37:37,265
I won't let him pass away before
paying for his deeds.

679
01:37:39,753 --> 01:37:41,889
Don't worry. He won't have an
easy death.

680
01:37:41,992 --> 01:37:45,586
Then, give me the word, Osman Bey.
Give me the word and I'll take his life.

681
01:37:46,012 --> 01:37:48,348
Let him pay for his sins.

682
01:37:48,458 --> 01:37:52,154
Now is not the time, Göktuğ.

683
01:37:52,985 --> 01:37:55,296
I can't get rid of Geyhatu
without his help.

684
01:37:55,960 --> 01:37:57,588
He needs to live a little longer.

685
01:37:58,342 --> 01:38:00,881
I talked to Balgay.

686
01:38:01,251 --> 01:38:03,534
His intention is having you
fight with Geyhatu.

687
01:38:03,916 --> 01:38:08,409
He dreams of killing you both after
you weaken him.

688
01:38:08,909 --> 01:38:12,844
I know, Göktuğ. But there still some
things I need to know.

689
01:38:14,114 --> 01:38:17,686
So, you will go to him.

690
01:38:20,200 --> 01:38:21,785
As you wish, Osman Bey.

691
01:38:21,785 --> 01:38:25,051
Göktuğ, your mission is difficult.

692
01:38:25,811 --> 01:38:29,702
You will be a companion to the killer of
your father and your people.

693
01:38:30,887 --> 01:38:34,727
This isn't a thing any warrior
can do.

694
01:38:36,178 --> 01:38:39,760
Your job is important.

695
01:38:42,889 --> 01:38:47,725
Because of the news you will bring,
many poor people will live in peace.

696
01:38:49,796 --> 01:38:53,990
But if...
If you say that you can't...

697
01:38:55,070 --> 01:38:57,397
...know that I won't despise you for that.

698
01:39:00,070 --> 01:39:02,801
My Bey, be at ease.

699
01:39:03,423 --> 01:39:07,019
I'll do whatever you order.

700
01:39:09,366 --> 01:39:10,360
Osman Bey.

701
01:39:11,630 --> 01:39:14,575
Protect my brother.

702
01:39:14,936 --> 01:39:17,529
Don't worry, Göktuğ.

703
01:39:18,003 --> 01:39:21,487
Your brother is my brother.

704
01:39:22,295 --> 01:39:23,519
Thank you.

705
01:39:23,952 --> 01:39:25,050
Thank you.

706
01:39:27,576 --> 01:39:31,207
May Allah help you on your way.

707
01:42:03,577 --> 01:42:05,259
Your father...

708
01:42:07,991 --> 01:42:09,778
...Oytun Alp...

709
01:42:11,957 --> 01:42:14,927
...when you were a baby...

710
01:42:15,618 --> 01:42:17,590
...at an ambush against me...

711
01:42:18,734 --> 01:42:20,669
...sacrificed himself.

712
01:42:25,091 --> 01:42:27,302
My Allah is witness...

713
01:42:30,191 --> 01:42:32,662
...if it wasn't for him...

714
01:42:34,484 --> 01:42:36,544
...I was going to die.

715
01:42:53,407 --> 01:42:55,842
He gave his last breath...

716
01:42:57,704 --> 01:42:59,790
...on me.

717
01:43:02,718 --> 01:43:05,139
He put his holy head...

718
01:43:06,263 --> 01:43:09,048
...on this knee of mine.

719
01:43:12,224 --> 01:43:14,426
He looked at me...

720
01:43:15,509 --> 01:43:19,014
...as if he was begging...

721
01:43:20,248 --> 01:43:22,901
...he looked at me as if he was begging...

722
01:43:23,786 --> 01:43:26,982
....but not because he was afraid...

723
01:43:27,441 --> 01:43:29,534
...not because of that...

724
01:43:31,536 --> 01:43:34,176
...his only concern was you.

725
01:43:41,314 --> 01:43:44,771
So, he looked at me like that...

726
01:43:46,742 --> 01:43:51,160
...my Burçin, he said. My orphan girl.

727
01:43:52,466 --> 01:43:54,359
Now...

728
01:43:55,722 --> 01:43:57,921
...she is an orphan.

729
01:44:01,277 --> 01:44:03,001
Burçin, he said...

730
01:44:05,855 --> 01:44:07,711
...is under your protection.

731
01:44:10,302 --> 01:44:12,768
Her head should be up, he said...

732
01:44:14,172 --> 01:44:16,823
...she is a daughter of a martyr, he said.

733
01:44:25,540 --> 01:44:27,624
On his last breath...

734
01:44:28,724 --> 01:44:31,382
...he wished for you, Burçin.

735
01:44:33,376 --> 01:44:36,014
He wished for you on his last breath.

736
01:44:44,349 --> 01:44:47,318
I didn't want anything to happen to him.

737
01:44:48,325 --> 01:44:50,060
I wouldn't want that.

738
01:44:50,945 --> 01:44:52,314
But it happened.

739
01:44:53,894 --> 01:44:57,638
And you spent whole your childhood...

740
01:44:58,095 --> 01:45:00,104
...with holding a grudge.

741
01:45:04,714 --> 01:45:07,590
I knew that you would never
forgive me.

742
01:45:09,476 --> 01:45:10,592
But...

743
01:45:12,300 --> 01:45:15,010
...but then you fell in love.

744
01:45:18,018 --> 01:45:19,990
You loved my Baybars.

745
01:45:21,370 --> 01:45:25,072
You looked at him like he
looked at you.

746
01:45:26,460 --> 01:45:29,917
Then, you grew up...

747
01:45:30,846 --> 01:45:33,318
...you came to kiss my hand.

748
01:45:34,634 --> 01:45:36,408
''Father, father!'' you said.

749
01:45:37,632 --> 01:45:40,153
You aren't responsible of anything.

750
01:45:41,590 --> 01:45:43,896
You raised me.

751
01:45:44,108 --> 01:45:46,308
You were a father to me, you said.

752
01:45:50,486 --> 01:45:52,666
I believed you.

753
01:45:54,854 --> 01:45:56,881
I swear, I believed you.

754
01:45:58,404 --> 01:46:00,580
I swear I did.

755
01:46:05,653 --> 01:46:07,784
I thought that the fire in your heart...

756
01:46:08,194 --> 01:46:10,705
...gone away for good.

757
01:46:14,337 --> 01:46:16,085
But...

758
01:46:16,850 --> 01:46:19,057
...I couldn't know that...

759
01:46:21,174 --> 01:46:23,520
...your grudge would revive after
his death.

760
01:46:25,993 --> 01:46:28,008
I couldn't know.

761
01:46:29,407 --> 01:46:32,664
I couldn't know, my daughter.

762
01:46:44,067 --> 01:46:45,342
Burçin.

763
01:46:46,375 --> 01:46:47,451
Burçin.

764
01:46:47,451 --> 01:46:48,798
My girl.

765
01:46:49,152 --> 01:46:51,466
Open your eyes, open your eyes!

766
01:46:53,088 --> 01:46:56,285
Come on, come on, open them.

767
01:47:02,358 --> 01:47:03,647
Father...

768
01:47:03,647 --> 01:47:07,158
Yes, my daughter, yes.
Yes, speak, my girl.

769
01:47:12,963 --> 01:47:15,445
Forgive me.

770
01:47:23,075 --> 01:47:25,817
My girl, open your eyes.

771
01:47:29,919 --> 01:47:32,614
My Burçin, open your eyes.

772
01:47:32,823 --> 01:47:35,663
Woman, woman, woman!
Come here!

773
01:47:36,122 --> 01:47:37,511
Come here at once!

774
01:47:40,272 --> 01:47:42,912
She opened her eyes!

775
01:47:43,423 --> 01:47:45,417
She spoke to me!
Then closed them again.

776
01:47:47,123 --> 01:47:49,932
Check her.
Check her.

777
01:47:49,932 --> 01:47:53,729
-I'll do what is needed.
-Yes, yes. Do what you need to do.

778
01:47:55,077 --> 01:47:57,868
Hang on, my girl. Hang on.

779
01:48:00,223 --> 01:48:05,633
Come on my Burçin.
Come on, come on.

780
01:48:08,641 --> 01:48:10,591
Come on.

781
01:48:13,349 --> 01:48:16,049
She is my daughter.

782
01:48:17,391 --> 01:48:21,981
Come on, my daughter, come on.

783
01:48:22,936 --> 01:48:25,266
Come on.

784
01:48:26,924 --> 01:48:31,464
Burçin, daughter.

785
01:48:32,347 --> 01:48:37,118
My Aybars, your fiancee...

786
01:48:37,118 --> 01:48:41,588
couldn't meet his lover, but...

787
01:48:41,627 --> 01:48:47,067
He will meet his eternal lover.

788
01:48:47,271 --> 01:48:51,701
Daughter, Burçin...

789
01:48:52,899 --> 01:48:56,809
your fate is...

790
01:48:58,381 --> 01:49:01,401
due to the last judgement.

791
01:49:15,451 --> 01:49:19,871
If it was a little bit stronger, it'd
destroy your liver.

792
01:49:21,978 --> 01:49:27,988
Erlik Han gave me an opportunity for
revenge.

793
01:49:30,285 --> 01:49:38,435
He gave me an opportunity to
take my soldiers...

794
01:49:38,665 --> 01:49:45,163
and show everyone who is in the power.

795
01:49:50,443 --> 01:49:52,823
Let's go.

796
01:50:16,430 --> 01:50:20,840
Commander Balgay, how is your wound?
Are you okay?

797
01:50:20,954 --> 01:50:25,626
- Rest a couple of days, if you want to.
- We don't have that much time.

798
01:50:25,626 --> 01:50:29,566
We are setting off with Cerkutay
as soon as possible.

799
01:50:30,173 --> 01:50:35,503
Tell me, why are you so late?
Where have you been?

800
01:50:35,968 --> 01:50:40,454
After I saved you, I followed Dündar
to ambush Dündar.

801
01:50:40,454 --> 01:50:45,064
But Osman acted before me,
and I returned.

802
01:50:52,902 --> 01:50:57,727
I owe you my life, Kongar.

803
01:50:57,727 --> 01:51:01,377
Wish anything from me.

804
01:51:01,377 --> 01:51:05,985
Revenge.
I wish for revenge, Commander Balgay.

805
01:51:05,985 --> 01:51:12,095
I wish to come with you to kill the ones
who disobey you.

806
01:51:17,418 --> 01:51:20,268
I have my full trust on you.

807
01:51:20,556 --> 01:51:25,346
You will stay here.
Keep a sharp scout.

808
01:51:49,756 --> 01:51:54,266
So, you wish to be with me.

809
01:51:54,397 --> 01:51:58,327
Okay then, you can come too.

810
01:51:58,381 --> 01:52:03,761
Our way is rough, and I am wounded.

811
01:52:03,936 --> 01:52:09,076
- You will have plenty to do.
- As you command, Commander Balgay.

812
01:52:17,083 --> 01:52:24,163
Then, let's go.
When we return, there will be a new era.

813
01:52:24,224 --> 01:52:26,264
Go!

814
01:52:56,176 --> 01:52:58,286
Traitor!

815
01:53:02,684 --> 01:53:06,184
Traitor!

816
01:54:01,145 --> 01:54:04,385
Traitor!

817
01:54:12,060 --> 01:54:14,750
Traitor!

818
01:54:33,965 --> 01:54:37,315
- Finish him, my Bey!
- Don't let him live!

819
01:54:53,494 --> 01:54:57,014
Alişar...

820
01:55:05,339 --> 01:55:08,629
Alişar!

821
01:55:10,892 --> 01:55:18,202
Alişar, who sold his soul to Mongols,
became their dog, and bossed around!

822
01:55:19,068 --> 01:55:21,318
Osman!

823
01:55:21,420 --> 01:55:25,325
You'll pay for what you've done, Osman!

824
01:55:25,325 --> 01:55:29,985
I will make you regret this!

825
01:55:30,218 --> 01:55:33,688
I will kill you all!

826
01:55:33,810 --> 01:55:36,220
Kill you all!

827
01:55:38,273 --> 01:55:41,233
Don't make me cut your toxic tongue!

828
01:55:42,465 --> 01:55:45,775
Don't make me cut your toxic tongue!

829
01:55:55,779 --> 01:56:00,099
This infidel was trying to...

830
01:56:00,611 --> 01:56:04,521
raid our tribe with his soldiers!

831
01:56:06,130 --> 01:56:13,740
In front of my father's blessed tribe,
he tried to call us account!

832
01:56:21,767 --> 01:56:26,667
Let everyone hear this!

833
01:56:27,210 --> 01:56:35,770
This devil is behind all of the
dirty cases.

834
01:56:40,378 --> 01:56:45,208
Batur's murderer is this dog.

835
01:56:45,512 --> 01:56:50,182
Murderer!
Damn you!

836
01:57:06,767 --> 01:57:11,547
As to my uncle Dündar, and Bahadır...

837
01:57:13,618 --> 01:57:19,918
They get egged on Alişar and
betrayed the Beys of the tribe.

838
01:57:21,447 --> 01:57:29,017
However, my father will decide
their fate.

839
01:57:54,033 --> 01:57:56,913
I am ashamed of tellling Aygül...

840
01:57:59,238 --> 01:58:03,368
what you have done.

841
01:58:06,621 --> 01:58:13,101
Now, go and tell everything to
your daughter.

842
01:58:15,267 --> 01:58:18,817
This shame will be enough for you, uncle.

843
01:58:21,499 --> 01:58:23,649
Go.

844
01:58:33,761 --> 01:58:39,321
Imprison him in a tent.
Put two Alps on him.

845
01:59:52,294 --> 01:59:55,944
- Father.
- My Bey.

846
02:00:19,182 --> 02:00:21,312
It's long.

847
02:00:21,635 --> 02:00:24,959
My husband is about to be executed,
you are doing nothing, father.

848
02:00:24,959 --> 02:00:29,989
Whatever it is, tell me right now.
Where is Alişar Bey? Where is my brother?

849
02:00:31,703 --> 02:00:37,731
Don't push your father, do whatever he
says. Let's go to our tent.

850
02:00:37,731 --> 02:00:40,691
Please, tell me father.

851
02:00:42,796 --> 02:00:45,396
What are you hiding?

852
02:00:45,405 --> 02:00:47,495
Batur's...

853
02:00:50,314 --> 02:00:53,354
Batur's murderer is...

854
02:00:55,596 --> 02:00:58,806
not Osman.

855
02:01:00,862 --> 02:01:03,012
Then who?

856
02:01:08,046 --> 02:01:11,246
Who?

857
02:01:20,141 --> 02:01:22,791
Alişar.

858
02:01:34,433 --> 02:01:36,873
It was Alişar.

859
02:02:10,073 --> 02:02:12,353
My Daughter.

860
02:02:27,605 --> 02:02:32,122
Did you send me to my brother's killer?

861
02:02:32,122 --> 02:02:38,082
Aygül, Aygül, daugher, don't do it.

862
02:02:38,410 --> 02:02:42,210
You are my reason, father.

863
02:02:42,225 --> 02:02:46,359
Daughter, don't do it Aygül.

864
02:02:46,359 --> 02:02:49,929
Please, don't do it, Aygül.

865
02:02:50,354 --> 02:02:54,224
Aygül!
Don't do it, daughter.

866
02:02:58,476 --> 02:03:00,846
Don't.

867
02:03:07,937 --> 02:03:10,077
Brother.

868
02:03:16,147 --> 02:03:21,027
Brother, brother.

869
02:04:17,459 --> 02:04:26,529
The blood of this dog, who bothered
our tribe, our valiants, our honor....

870
02:04:27,899 --> 02:04:33,779
Our Bey deserves it.

871
02:04:57,196 --> 02:05:01,256
Before me, this privilege...

872
02:05:02,058 --> 02:05:09,378
is my brother Osman's right, he
brought him into line.

873
02:06:28,435 --> 02:06:30,806
Osman Bey.

874
02:06:30,806 --> 02:06:35,016
You'll be a trouble for your tribe
as well.

875
02:06:35,684 --> 02:06:40,424
Don't do it, we can talk,
come to an agreement.

876
02:06:41,146 --> 02:06:45,333
This is bannerlord talking to you.

877
02:06:45,333 --> 02:06:48,833
The penalty for this will be rough.

878
02:06:50,446 --> 02:06:59,226
Think it through, only I can save you
from Geyhatu.

879
02:07:05,369 --> 02:07:15,089
The only power that can protect us is
my Lord.

880
02:07:20,349 --> 02:07:25,629
You can't even protect your honor.

881
02:07:46,785 --> 02:07:51,915
Osman Bey, don't, listen to me.

882
02:07:53,947 --> 02:07:57,617
Listen to me, listen to me.

883
02:07:58,724 --> 02:08:03,914
Look, we can come to an agreement,
listen to me.

884
02:08:55,724 --> 02:09:00,834
Geyhatu's dogs.
They smelt the blood.

885
02:09:11,516 --> 02:09:14,656
Sufutay.

886
02:09:15,079 --> 02:09:20,099
I am Noyan Sufutay.

887
02:09:20,729 --> 02:09:25,469
I am here as the messenger of
blessed Geyhatu.

888
02:09:32,904 --> 02:09:38,424
Release Bannerlord Alişar right now.

889
02:09:43,951 --> 02:09:51,121
And deliver me that rebel Osman.

890
02:09:51,319 --> 02:09:56,109
Otherwise, not only Kayıs...

891
02:09:56,124 --> 02:10:01,964
but all the tribes in this land...

892
02:10:02,112 --> 02:10:05,372
will be slaughtered.

893
02:10:13,229 --> 02:10:16,429
Noyan Sufutay.

894
02:10:18,657 --> 02:10:21,857
I am Gündüz Bey.

895
02:10:22,007 --> 02:10:26,847
We die one, resurrect a thousand.

896
02:10:27,989 --> 02:10:34,059
However, we are not delivering
my brother Osman Bey.

897
02:10:39,119 --> 02:10:48,909
Are you disobeying the order
of blessed Geyhatu?

898
02:10:48,920 --> 02:10:58,540
Damn Geyhatu. Is he bigger than Türk's
laws to ask me to forgive this dog?

899
02:11:01,239 --> 02:11:06,129
Geyhatu doesn't ask, Geyhatu orders,
Osman Bey.

900
02:11:08,195 --> 02:11:15,925
We trampled your laws when we
conquered Konya.

901
02:11:23,985 --> 02:11:29,325
In this tribe,
there will be my wedding tomorrow.

902
02:11:29,950 --> 02:11:34,690
Tell Geyhatu, if he is to take my life,
let him come.

903
02:11:36,348 --> 02:11:40,208
Kayıs are not like the ones who sells
their freedom...

904
02:11:40,502 --> 02:11:47,372
just to live, and give up on their honor.

905
02:11:48,602 --> 02:11:52,512
If he is strong enough to rule us...

906
02:11:53,426 --> 02:11:56,436
let him come!

907
02:11:58,354 --> 02:12:03,064
Are you challanging Geyhatu,
Dark Osman?!

908
02:12:13,560 --> 02:12:19,170
Forgiving cruels is cruelity
for the oppressed.

909
02:12:20,341 --> 02:12:24,631
Neither our tradition nor our religion
approve this.

910
02:12:28,115 --> 02:12:32,765
Now, tell Geyhatu.

911
02:13:17,421 --> 02:13:22,621
From now on, in this lands we conquered...

912
02:13:23,843 --> 02:13:26,383
there will no longer be cruelity.

913
02:13:34,670 --> 02:13:40,770
Justice forever,
Freedom forever!

914
02:13:40,770 --> 02:14:54,972
Allah-u Ekber
(Allah is the greatest)

915
02:14:57,224 --> 02:15:00,494
Allah-u Ekber
(Allah is the greatest)

916
02:15:00,764 --> 02:15:26,314
Please contact turkision@gmail.com
for any inquiries